# {app}

<!-- One paragraph: what this application is, who uses it, and what it talks to. -->

A CF application. Its own classes are `{prefix}`-prefixed (`{prefix}Model`, `{prefix}Utils`);
framework classes stay `C`-prefixed.

Framework-wide conventions are deliberately **not** repeated here — soft delete on `status`,
the PHP 7.4 ceiling, code style, `phpcf` commands, and the rest live in the docroot's own
`CLAUDE.md`, one level above this directory. Write down only what is true of {app} and
nothing else; a copy of the framework rules here would be a second copy to keep in sync, and
it would drift.

